  "final_answer": "## Recipe Found: Easy Vegetarian Spinach Lasagna\n\nI found a vegetarian lasagna recipe on Allrecipes that meets all your criteria. Here are the details:\n\n### Recipe Overview\n- **Title:** Easy Vegetarian Spinach Lasagna\n- **URL:** https://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/229764/easy-vegetarian-spinach-lasagna/\n- **Rating:** 4.6 out of 5 stars ✓ (exceeds 4.5 minimum)\n- **Ratings Count:** 117 ✓ (exceeds 100 reviews)\n- **Servings:** 6 ✓ (exactly matches your requirement)\n- **Submitted by:** MOTTSBELA\n- **Prep Time:** 20 mins | **Cook Time:** 1 hr | **Total Time:** 1 hr 25 mins\n\n### Description\nSatisfying layers of stretchy melted mozzarella, creamy ricotta, and spinach combine with sauce-coated lasagna noodles for the ultimate comfort food.\n\n### Ingredients\n- Cooking spray\n- Salt and ground black pepper to taste\n- 10 ounces fresh spinach\n- 9 lasagna noodles\n- 1 (8 ounce) container ricotta cheese\n- 1 cup shredded mozzarella cheese, divided\n- 1 large egg, lightly beaten\n- 1 pinch ground nutmeg\n- 1 pinch dried basil\n- 1 cup pasta sauce\n- ¼ cup grated Parmesan cheese\n\n### Directions\n1. Preheat the oven to 400°F (200°C). Spray a 1½-quart casserole dish with cooking spray.\n2. Bring a large pot of lightly salted water to a boil. Place spinach in the water and boil until wilted and tender, about 2 minutes. Remove spinach with a slotted spoon, pressing out excess water. Set aside.\n3. Cook lasagna noodles in the same boiling water, stirring occasionally, about 8 minutes. Drain.\n4. Mix spinach, ricotta cheese, ½ cup shredded mozzarella, egg, nutmeg, basil, salt, and black pepper in a bowl.\n5. Spread ¼ cup pasta sauce on the bottom of the dish. Layer 3 noodles, half the ricotta mixture, and ¼ cup sauce. Repeat layers. End with remaining 3 noodles and ¼ cup sauce. Top with remaining ½ cup mozzarella and Parmesan. Cover with foil.\n6. Bake covered for 25 minutes. Uncover and bake another 25 minutes until bubbling and browned. Let stand 5 minutes before serving.\n\n### Nutrition (per serving)\n305 calories | 10g fat | 37g carbs | 18g protein\n\nThis was the best match among the candidates. Other high-rated vegetarian lasagnas I checked (like the Vegetarian Four Cheese Lasagna with 243 ratings) didn't qualify because they serve 8 instead of 6.",
